    {
      "id": "EX-realization-change",
      "title": "More explicit wording can still request the same failed operation",
      "path": "knowledge/staged/experience-full-maintenance-20261101/entries/realization-change.md",
      "version": 1,
      "sha256": "3264718a666309c6b9506907a0b15774d300def5719a25015120a8a42231e1e6",
      "summary": "A new prompt is a new hypothesis only to the extent that it changes something relevant to the failure. Specifying a missing relation, relocating an effect and restating an already explicit operation test different propositions.",
      "questions": [
        "Did the proposed alternative actually change the failed operation?"
      ],
      "renderers": [
        "bernini",
        "ditto"
      ],
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-B-003",
        "EV-H-D-benchmark__003__short",
        "EV-H-D-024__long__full_knowledge",
        "EV-H-D-benchmark__001__long",
        "EV-H-B-benchmark__001__long",
        "EV-F001",
        "EV-F003"
      ],
      "review_status": "draft",
      "review_reference": "pending_user_content_review"
    },
    {
      "id": "EX-part-binding",
      "title": "Getting the attribute right can still modify the wrong referent",
      "path": "knowledge/staged/experience-full-maintenance-20261101/entries/part-binding.md",
      "version": 1,
      "sha256": "ab6a45951c20a8d26f76004835924ba5c07d1677705534dc34ccca988826c7a2",
      "summary": "A correct attribute on the wrong part is a binding failure. Asking for more of the attribute can strengthen the wrong realization rather than move it to the intended place.",
      "questions": [
        "Why did the correct effect appear on the wrong part?"
      ],
      "renderers": [
        "bernini",
        "ditto"
      ],
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-F004",
        "EV-H-B-fewshot_004__long__no_knowledge",
        "EV-D-027-full",
        "EV-H-B-027__short__no_knowledge"
      ],
      "review_status": "draft",
      "review_reference": "pending_user_content_review"
    },
    {
      "id": "EX-wanted-state",
      "title": "A correction needs a positive visual account of the replacement",
      "path": "knowledge/staged/experience-full-maintenance-20261101/entries/wanted-state.md",
      "version": 1,
      "sha256": "225c319c105a402aca2cacc4c69588fa6bd3629a17d4e2d1e9dc6dc05d7c228f",
      "summary": "A removal request identifies dissatisfaction, but may leave the replacement appearance underspecified or in conflict with the surrounding design. Describe how the wanted state fits that design.",
      "questions": [
        "What visual state replaces the unwanted artifact?"
      ],
      "renderers": [
        "bernini",
        "ditto"
      ],
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-H-D-benchmark__001__short",
        "EV-H-D-027__short__no_knowledge",
        "EV-F004",
        "EV-H-B-fewshot_004__long__no_knowledge"
      ],
      "review_status": "draft",
      "review_reference": "pending_user_content_review"
    },
    {
      "id": "EX-style-realization",
      "title": "Style specificity is a system of visible relationships",
      "path": "knowledge/staged/experience-full-maintenance-20261101/entries/style-realization.md",
      "version": 1,
      "sha256": "dee95f5f052aa2cd093f83d3b4adff3d80cf2de7d8ecc34dd6b99eef79a9a268",
      "summary": "Concrete style knowledge is useful when it explains how visible elements produce the effect: how marks construct tone, material responds to light, or ornament fits a silhouette. A longer inventory can still miss the defining relationship.",
      "questions": [
        "What does style knowledge add beyond a genre label?"
      ],
      "renderers": [
        "bernini",
        "ditto"
      ],
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-H-D-benchmark__001__long",
        "EV-F003"
      ],
      "review_status": "draft",
      "review_reference": "pending_user_content_review"
    },
    {
      "id": "EX-environment-replacement",
      "title": "Theme cues and a reconstructed place are different achievements",
      "path": "knowledge/staged/experience-full-maintenance-20261101/entries/environment-replacement.md",
      "version": 1,
      "sha256": "56b666f1d14ad148f6b2da0f4a59f2b69c8a568d433b262301618ce8cd106904",
      "summary": "A few highly recognizable motifs can establish a theme while the source environment still determines most of the place. Judge what carries the scene, not just whether the requested nouns appear.",
      "questions": [
        "Why does the scene have theme cues but remain the old place?"
      ],
      "renderers": [
        "bernini",
        "ditto"
      ],
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-F004",
        "EV-F005",
        "EV-F006",
        "EV-F007",
        "EV-F001",
        "EV-D-FS4-full"
      ],
      "review_status": "draft",
      "review_reference": "pending_user_content_review"
    },
    {
      "id": "EX-lighting-integration",
      "title": "A visible lamp, an emissive accent and illumination of the scene are separate",
      "path": "knowledge/staged/experience-full-maintenance-20261101/entries/lighting-integration.md",
      "version": 1,
      "sha256": "c839526fafec19aee4f5855277d272dea0d1ece632df8749bd1ce8c88af96096",
      "summary": "Lighting style depends on relationships among sources, receivers, shadows and reflections. Adding a lamp or a glowing edge can satisfy a local cue while leaving the scene under its original illumination.",
      "questions": [
        "Why are lamps and glows present without the intended atmosphere?"
      ],
      "renderers": [
        "bernini",
        "ditto"
      ],
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-F002",
        "EV-F004",
        "EV-F005",
        "EV-F007",
        "EV-H-D-benchmark__001__short"
      ],
      "review_status": "draft",
      "review_reference": "pending_user_content_review"
    },
    {
      "id": "EX-time-binding",
      "title": "An attribute appearing in a clip is different from an attribute persisting through it",
      "path": "knowledge/staged/experience-full-maintenance-20261101/entries/time-binding.md",
      "version": 1,
      "sha256": "121501acec56f9f6f56ef8947c41d9b779b7d4c526442dd1ed54e1eda898c194",
      "summary": "Appearance, persistence and event timing answer different questions. A convincing opening can conceal a later loss; a stable-looking face can still perform a different emotional action.",
      "questions": [
        "Did the design persist, and did the original event persist?"
      ],
      "renderers": [
        "bernini",
        "ditto"
      ],
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-F006",
        "EV-F005",
        "EV-F001",
        "EV-H-B-benchmark__001__long",
        "EV-batch-facts",
        "EV-visual-inspection"
      ],
      "review_status": "draft",
      "review_reference": "pending_user_content_review"
    },
    {
      "id": "EX-continuation-value",
      "title": "The value of a revision depends on the gap it closes and the alternative already available",
      "path": "knowledge/staged/experience-full-maintenance-20261101/entries/continuation-value.md",
      "version": 1,
      "sha256": "48171911b195062943debea5defb906482d92f4eedc64c3cec196700714d0c99",
      "summary": "A new result may fix the latest complaint yet be a worse answer to the original request. Evaluate the consequential gap and the retained alternatives, rather than counting verdicts or following the most recent comparison.",
      "questions": [
        "Is a repaired complaint enough to justify another attempt or a final choice?"
      ],
      "renderers": [
        "bernini",
        "ditto"
      ],
